eLinkedRoots`, `refuseForeign`, `checkRepoConfig`), each of which it must be given when `openRepo` gains one. Only a name with nothing at it is gone: the places that decide whether a repository is there, or which entry and proposal files it holds (the two roots, a repository's name, its `entries/` and `proposals/` folders and the names in them), ask the disk with `lookAt`, `kindAt` and `namesIn` (`repo.ts`), for which anything that cannot be looked at is a refusal, never "not there"; `doctor` lists the folders with the same three. The older `isDirectory` and `existsOnDisk` read any failure to look as "no" and are used only inside a repository, behind one of those refusals: never decide a repository's presence with them. A link or a file where a repository's folder was is refused by name and its index rows stay, and a project's row names its folder while anything is at that name (`matchProject` in `resolve.ts`), so no state of the disk gives a project a second folder. The index belongs to one data directory: `rebuild` refuses, forgetting nothing, where there is no `knowledge/` folder and the index holds repositories. An interrupted operation is put back by its intent record, path by path, only where a file is still as the engine left it; a record is read only when every path in it is the store's own (`ownPath`), and a path is followed only through real folders (`reachedByFolders`). Three rules live in one place each: the write of the engine's own text, with its record and its undo, in `commitChange` (`repo.ts`; `adopt` keeps its own frame in `store.ts`, since it gives a person's bytes back instead of restoring from HEAD); a step of `openRepo` under the repository's lease in `underOwnLease` (`repo.ts`); a command over several repositories, where one the store refuses is set aside, in `inEachRepo` (`index-store.ts`, with `isRefusal` in `errors.ts`). An agent's write is a proposal until a person accepts it; the entry point passes the writer, never the caller. A module's